# The delayed ability Nafs Asp's trigger makes is controlled by the Asp's controller, Bot1, not by the player it is about
# (CR 603.7e). At the beginning of Bot2's draw step it triggers with Bot2's Howling Mine, and the active player's goes on
# the stack first (CR 101.4): the Asp's is on top, Bot1's, and Bot2 is asked to order nothing.
[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Nafs Asp
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Howling Mine
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nafs Asp.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Howling Mine.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Nafs Asp)
[T4 Bot2.Draw]
? Stack = Nafs Asp; Howling Mine
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
